beginning in fort erie ontario a number  of trucks slow rolled their way to the  niagara region sunday morning this is  not just for the truckers  this is the backbone they are they are  the backbone of canada  and the canadian and american good  freedom freedom protests like these come  as convoys across the country are  heading to ottawa to oppose a vaccine  mandate which requires truckers  traveling back and forth across the u.s  border to be immunized against coba 19.  sylvan charlebois says the mandate is  coming at the wrong time he fears it  will drive up the price of consumer  goods i think we're at a point now  in in the pandemic that we need to  strike a more functional balance between  saving lives and keeping canadians fed  the latest pushback on vaccine mandates  from truck drivers draws a parallel with  canada's ongoing divide over public  health restrictions it prompts the  question as to whether policy is  matching the science rather than chasing  down the unvaccinated we should be  pushing our governments  to deal with the global health risk  that's in front of all of us bioethicist  carrie bowman believes the government  should focus on vaccinating the rest of  the world instead of the holdouts in  canada others such as dr isaac bogot say  policymakers shouldn't keep measures in  place longer than necessary whenever a  policy is being implemented i think we  have to ask ourselves what's the goal  here like what are you actually trying  to do both agree there should be  flexibility in how pandemic policy is  shaped in the future that's probably one  of the most important aspects  to question when you're making policy  and sadly i think sometimes that gets  lost brittany rosen global news toronto
 

